do CelyneLoop.play_bgm()
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/PART OF YOUR WORLD.png" fade="0.0"]
join Seyche left [animation="Bounce In" length="0.0"]
join Celyna right [animation="Bounce In" length="0.0"]
As days blurred into hours for the goddesses, an unexpected warmth enveloped them.[pause=0.6] Unforced and achingly familiar.[pause=0.8] It was as if it had always lingered there,[pause=0.3] waiting.[pause=0.5] Waiting patiently for a thousand years.
The sea lit up with a brilliant blue glow, like stars dancing along with the waves like reflections of the night sky. [pause=0.8]They sat by the shore, side by side, admiring the view above and before them.
Seyche’s eyes never left Celyna, marveling at details of the moon goddess’s features. [pause=0.6]The twinkle in her hair,[pause=0.4] the way her graceful form complimented the night.[pause=0.6] How the light of her presence balanced the shadows, as if the galaxies itself leaned in to admire her.
Celyna: Is there something you wish to ask, dear?
update Seyche (Surprised) [fade="Fade Cross" fade_length="0.0"]
Seyche: [lspeed=0.2]!!
Seyche: Wha-[pause=0.7] no![pause=0.5] [lspeed=0.1]I mean... no, sorry. [pause=0.2]I was...
Celyna: No need to apologize.
Celyna: Though it seems like you have something in your mind.
Seyche (Uncomfortable): Oh… [pause=0.6][lspeed=0.1]I was just… [pause=0.4]thinking.
Celyna: Of what, dear?
The sea goddess took a pause,[pause=0.2] the question seemed so simple yet she couldn’t really say what she had in mind.[pause=0.5] Because really,[pause=0.1] even though they had just first met,[pause=0.1] everything seemed so familiar.[pause=0.5] But she had no recollection of anything.
The days spent together felt effortless, as though it had always been that way.[pause=0.4] Seyche didn’t answer right away, she only shook her head, brushing away her thoughts while shifting her gaze towards the view before her.
Seyche (Normal): I forgot about it already.
update Celyna (Giggle) [length="1.5"]
An occasional chuckle came from Celyna after Seyche’s reply before returning to their comfortable silence.[pause=0.6] Some things don't always change from the past.
At least...
That’s what Celyna hoped.